From: Daniel Pawlik <pawlik.dan@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mac80211: use netdev_hw_addr_list_count() on Linux 7.4

Linux 7.4 made the count member of struct netdev_hw_addr_list private
(renamed to _count) and introduced the netdev_hw_addr_list_count()
accessor, which is what mainline mac80211 uses since then. Keep the
direct member access for older kernels the backports still build
against.

--- a/net/mac80211/driver-ops.h
+++ b/net/mac80211/driver-ops.h
@@ -188,5 +188,9 @@
 	u64 ret = 0;
 
+#if LINUX_VERSION_IS_GEQ(7,4,0)
+	trace_drv_prepare_multicast(local, netdev_hw_addr_list_count(mc_list));
+#else
 	trace_drv_prepare_multicast(local, mc_list->count);
+#endif
 
 	if (local->ops->prepare_multicast)
